//! What the codemod knows about the widgets of `compose_rust::ui::next`.
//!
//! The function forms are generated by `macro_rules!` in `ui/next/*.rs`, so their
//! signatures cannot be read from the source with a parser. This table holds the few
//! things the rewrite cannot derive from the chain itself: which widgets there are, the
//! handler that becomes a required positional argument, the argument types an optional
//! handler's closure has to spell out inside `Some(..)`, and the methods that changed
//! name. Everything else maps one to one: a builder method becomes the parameter of the
//! same name, and a wrong name is a compile error at the rewritten call.

/// A widget whose main handler moved to a required positional argument right after the
/// data, with the closure written when the chain never set it.
pub struct MainHandler {
    pub widget: &'static str,
    pub method: &'static str,
    pub empty: &'static str,
}

